CAT = "dkBasics"; SEG = "BAS"
Q = [
("Where do the Danish traffic rules (færdselsloven) apply?",
 "Anywhere with general traffic", ["Only on public roads and streets", "Only outside built-up areas", "Only on roads owned by the state"],
 "The rules apply on all streets, roads, cycle tracks, pavements, squares, bridges, tunnels and paths with general traffic, whether public or private."),
('At Danish road works, which colour are the temporary lane markings that you follow?',
 'Yellow', ['Orange', 'Blue', 'Red'],
 'Yellow markings are used for temporary control, for example at road works, and must be followed instead of the white lines.'),
("An officer in a yellow vest stands in a junction in Odense and beckons you forward, but your signal is red. Who decides?",
 "The officer", ["The red light", "The give-way sign", "The car in front"],
 "Police directions come before signs, markings, signals and the ordinary rules, so you follow the officer's signal."),
("Which vehicle may you drive with a category B licence?",
 "A van of 3,500 kg", ["A minibus for 12 passengers", "A lorry of 7,500 kg", "A car with a 3,500 kg trailer"],
 "Category B covers cars and vans up to 3,500 kg permitted total weight, seating at most 8 passengers besides the driver."),
("With category B, what is the heaviest trailer you may always tow, whatever the car weighs?",
 "750 kg", ["500 kg", "1,000 kg", "3,500 kg"],
 "A trailer of up to 750 kg permitted total weight is always allowed. A heavier one is allowed if car and trailer together do not exceed 3,500 kg permitted total weight."),
("According to the Danish rules, what is the only lawful reason to sound your horn?",
 "To warn of danger", ["To greet someone you know", "To hurry a slow driver", "To thank another driver"],
 "Short use of the horn or a flash of the headlights is only for warning of danger. Any other use of the horn is forbidden."),
("You need to warn another road user of danger after dark. What should you normally use?",
 "A flash of the headlights", ["A long blast of the horn", "Your hazard warning lights", "Your rear fog light"],
 "In the lighting-up time you warn with a light signal instead of the horn, unless the danger is immediate."),
("When is the lighting-up time (lygtetændingstid)?",
 "Sunset to sunrise or low light", ["From 22:00 to 06:00 every day", "From 1 November to 31 March", "Only once street lights are on"],
 "Lighting-up time runs from sunset to sunrise, and also whenever darkness, fog, mist, rain or similar make lights necessary. Then use at least dipped beam."),
("In daylight, which lights may replace dipped beam while driving?",
 "Daytime running lights", ["Parking lights on their own", "No lights at all", "Hazard warning lights"],
 "Outside the lighting-up time you must drive with dipped beam, but daytime running lights or front fog lights may be used instead."),
('You have a green light at a junction when an ambulance with blue lights and siren approaches from a side road. What must you do?',
 'Let it pass, even on green', ['Go, as your light is green', 'Speed up out of its way', 'Stop inside the junction'],
 'You must give free passage to emergency vehicles using blue lights and siren, even when your light is green. Stop or move aside without creating danger.'),
("Your 9-year-old nephew is 128 cm tall. In Denmark, what must he sit in or on in your car?",
 "An approved child restraint", ["The adult seat belt alone", "Any cushion from home", "Nothing, he is over 3"],
 "Children under 135 cm must use a child seat or other approved restraint suited to their height and weight, such as a booster with the belt, instead of the seat belt alone."),
("You drive your daughter's football team home. Who must make sure the players under 15 are belted in?",
 "The driver", ["The players themselves", "The players' parents", "The team coach"],
 "The driver is responsible for passengers under 15 using a seat belt or other approved restraint."),
("You want to put your baby's rear-facing seat on the front passenger seat. What must be true?",
 "The airbag is off", ["The baby is asleep", "The trip is under 10 km", "The seat is pushed back"],
 "A rear-facing child seat must never be used in front of an active front airbag. Switch the airbag off or use another seat."),
("A load sticks out more than 1 m behind your car. What must you do?",
 "Mark the end of the load", ["Drive with hazard lights on", "Nothing on short trips", "Drive at 30 km/h"],
 "Loads sticking out more than 1 m at the front or rear, or more than 15 cm at the sides, must be clearly marked; after dark with lights as well."),
("Your engine dies on a country road where your car blocks part of the lane. How far back does the warning triangle go?",
 "At least 50 m before the car", ["At least 10 m before the car", "On the car's roof", "At least 100 m after the car"],
 "On ordinary roads the warning triangle goes at least 50 m before the car; on motorways at least 100 m. Hazard lights may be used as well."),
("You tow a broken-down car with a rope. What is the highest speed allowed?",
 "30 km/h", ["20 km/h", "50 km/h", "80 km/h"],
 "When towing, the gap may be at most 4 m (mark the rope if it is over 2 m), the towed car needs a licensed driver, and the speed limit is 30 km/h."),
("You are involved in a collision, even if it was not your fault. What must you do?",
 "Stop and help the injured", ["Drive on if nobody is hurt", "Leave before police arrive", "Only phone your insurer"],
 "You must stop at once and help anyone injured, and give your name and address to others involved if they ask."),
("You call 112 after a crash. What should you tell them first?",
 "Where the crash happened", ["The colour of your car", "Who you think was to blame", "The name of your insurer"],
 "Tell the emergency centre where it happened, any special dangers, how many are hurt and whether anyone's life is at risk, and where you are calling from."),
("Which insurance must the owner of a car have?",
 "Liability insurance", ["Comprehensive cover", "Travel insurance", "Breakdown cover"],
 "The owner or long-term user of a motor vehicle must have compulsory liability insurance to cover claims for damage caused to others."),
("A friend wants to borrow your car but has no valid licence. May you lend it?",
 "No, it is forbidden", ["Yes, for a short trip", "Yes, if you sit beside them", "Yes, on private roads only"],
 "It is forbidden to let anyone drive a vehicle without a valid licence for it."),
("How much pure alcohol is one standard drink (genstand) in Denmark?",
 "12 g", ["6 g", "20 g", "33 g"],
 "One standard drink is 12 g of pure alcohol, about one 33 cl lager, a 12 cl glass of wine or a 4 cl glass of spirits."),
("You were at a party in Aarhus until 2 a.m. and plan to drive to work at 8. What is true?",
 "It may still be too high", ["Sleep has burned it all off", "Coffee will make you sober", "A cold shower will clear it"],
 "Nothing speeds up the breakdown of alcohol: not sleep, exercise or coffee. A person of 60 kg needs about 1.5 to 2 hours for each drink."),
("Above 30 km/h, you drive 10% faster. What happens to the risk of a fatal crash?",
 "It can rise by up to 45%", ["It rises by about 10% too", "It does not change at all", "It rises by only about 5%"],
 "Above 30 km/h, a 10% increase in speed can raise the risk of a fatal crash by up to 45%. Speed is a major factor in crashes and injuries."),
("Why should you always wear a seat belt, even on short trips at low speed?",
 "You cannot brace even at 10 km/h", ["It is only needed on motorways", "The airbag does the same job", "It only matters for passengers"],
 "Even at speeds under 10 km/h you cannot hold yourself in place with your arms. Most belt-free injuries happen on ordinary short trips."),
]
